  "client_view_text": " A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked over to investigate, his boots sinking into the damp sand.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and pulled out A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic crash of the waves against the shore, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, its glassy surface glinting in the sunlight.\n\nCurious, Jack picked up the bottle and examined it. It was old, the cork worn and weathered, but the paper inside was still intact. He carefully pulled out the message, and his eyes scanned the words scrawled on the page.\n\n\"Dear whoever finds this,\" the message read, \"I am writing to you from a place of great sorrow. My name is Emily, and I am a sailor's wife. My husband, James, set sail on a voyage to the Far East, but he never returned. I have been waiting for him for five years, and I fear I shall never see him again. I am sending this message to the sea, in the hope that it will find its way to someone who can tell me the truth about James's fate. If you are reading this, please, please tell me"
}